## Session Start — MANDATORY

**Complete these steps BEFORE writing any code. Skipping any step = Task Failure.**

### Entry Verification

Your **first message** for any implementation task MUST include actual output from:

```bash
$ invar guard --changed
$ invar map --top 10
```

No output = Session not started correctly. Stop, run commands, restart.

### Context Loading

1. Read INVAR.md (protocol definition)
2. Read .invar/examples/ (Core/Shell patterns — **must read**)
3. Read .invar/context.md (project state, lessons learned)

### Why This Matters

- `invar guard` detects existing violations — don't build on broken foundation
- `invar map` shows code structure — know where to add new code
- Examples and context provide project-specific patterns

Skipping these → Non-compliant code → Rework required → Time wasted

